From 4981be61fa465f38e45802489ee47e6bb1f70b58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Gre=C5=84?= <witold.gren@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:10:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtsp: refuse a PLAY that gst-rtsp-server would abort on

A live view that gives up on a silent camera ends its sources with EOS. When a client's PLAY
was waiting for the camera's next frame at that moment (the media had been suspended after
DESCRIBE, which drops what had streamed), the PLAY went on without a segment and
gst_rtsp_media_get_rates aborted the whole process ("complete stream without rate", an
assertion in GStreamer 1.22): every camera was gone until a restart. The client class's
adjust_play_mode, which runs just before that check, now answers such a PLAY with 503 Service
Unavailable and the client retries.
---
 src/rtsp/gst/server.rs | 151 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 148 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

